WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.120
Proposition two changes how California saves for bad

2
00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:03.860
budget years.

3
00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:07.260
Current rules stop requiring additional deposits when that

4
00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:10.440
account reaches ten percent of General Fund tax

5
00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:10.720
revenues.

6
00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:14.560
Proposition two raises that threshold to twenty percent

7
00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:18.340
and requires more saving in particularly strong

8
00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:19.740
investment-tax years.

9
00:00:20.033 --> 00:00:21.753
It changes the rules over time;

10
00:00:22.473 --> 00:00:24.653
it does not instantly double the money already

11
00:00:24.653 --> 00:00:25.153
saved.

12
00:00:25.447 --> 00:00:28.447
The measure also extends required extra debt payments

13
00:00:28.447 --> 00:00:32.207
from twenty thirty through twenty forty, and expands

14
00:00:32.207 --> 00:00:34.267
the debts those payments can address.

15
00:00:34.573 --> 00:00:37.353
A voter might prefer a stronger buffer against

16
00:00:37.353 --> 00:00:38.193
service cuts,

17
00:00:38.793 --> 00:00:42.293
emergency borrowing, or tax increases during a downturn.

18
00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:45.740
Another voter could prioritize services or infrastructure

19
00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:46.240
now.

20
00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:50.260
Yes changes reserve and extra-debt-payment rules;

21
00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:52.560
no keeps the current rules.

22
00:00:53.247 --> 00:00:55.287
Visit our website for the fuller explanation, source

23
00:00:55.287 --> 00:00:56.327
links, and official

24
00:00:56.847 --> 00:00:57.567
voter guide.
